{
"content_id": "133001",
"reference_id": 109055,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "1 Peter 5:1–5",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "60005001-60005005",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<p>Peter described <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132064\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">church elders</data> and leaders as <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132224\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">shepherds</data> over God’s people.</p><p>His instructions to them were like Jesus’ instructions to his <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"131986\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">disciples</data> in Luke 22:24–30.</p><p>Church leaders mustn’t act proud or act like rulers. Jesus is the Chief Shepherd and they must obey him.</p><p>They must follow Jesus’ example of being a <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"132005\" data-resource-code=\"BiblicaStudyNotesKeyTerms\" data-language=\"eng\">leader who served</data>.</p><p>Leaders who serve faithfully will share Jesus’ glory when he returns to earth.</p><p>Other believers must respect and follow leaders who lead like Jesus.</p>",
